<%# The drop affordance for composer-drop.

    composer-drop accepts a file dropped anywhere on the page, because the composer is
    the only thing on the page that takes one. This overlay is what tells the user
    where it is going, so it has to sit over the whole region that reads as "the
    composer" — its parent must be positioned (`relative`, or a `fixed` panel).

    pointer-events-none keeps it out of the way of the controls underneath, and
    aria-hidden keeps a purely visual drag cue out of the accessibility tree.

    Locals: message — the sentence to show. inset — the Tailwind inset utility. %>
<% inset ||= "inset-0" %>
<div data-composer-drop-target="overlay"
     aria-hidden="true"
     class="hidden absolute <%= inset %> z-30 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg border-2 border-dashed border-indigo-500 bg-indigo-50/95 pointer-events-none">
  <span class="text-sm font-medium text-indigo-700 px-4 text-center"><%= message %></span>
</div>
